WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:18.019
The weeks leading up to the big event passed like mere minutes and before they could catch their breath, the eve of Meg's wedding day was upon them.

2
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:25.954
The girls changed into their pajamas but nobody felt like sleeping because this was the last evening that Meg would spend with them.

3
00:00:25.955 --> 00:00:32.190
"This time tomorrow, you will be a married woman," Amy stated as she brushed Meg's hair.

4
00:00:32.191 --> 00:00:36.603
"Are you nervous?" asked Beth, laying her hand over Meg's.

5
00:00:36.604 --> 00:00:44.106
"No," said Meg with a smile. "After such a long engagement, John and I can't wait to be married."

6
00:00:44.107 --> 00:00:49.322
"Have you already forgotten about us then?" Jo pouted childishly.

7
00:00:49.323 --> 00:00:56.656
"Of course not, Jo," Meg said gently, extending a hand, which Jo diverted her eyes from and turned away.

8
00:00:56.657 --> 00:01:00.441
"I'm going to miss you girls very much," Meg continued.

9
00:01:00.442 --> 00:01:06.852
"But since I'll live just down the road, I'll expect daily visits so that we'll always remain in close touch."

10
00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:14.730
The sisters, including Jo, encircled Meg and after many sniffles, cries, and loving words, they went off to bed.

11
00:01:14.731 --> 00:01:21.153
Several hours later as Jo was lying wide awake in the dark, she felt a familiar hand on her shoulder.

12
00:01:21.154 --> 00:01:28.587
"Jo?" whispered Meg as she slid over to her sister and held Jo's hand as they did when they were little girls.

13
00:01:30.038 --> 00:01:34.148
"I'm going to miss you, Meg," Jo whispered tearfully.

14
00:01:34.149 --> 00:01:39.410
"Me too," replied Meg. "Take care of the girls, Jo."

15
00:01:39.411 --> 00:01:45.836
Nodding, Jo squeezed Meg's hand and the two sisters fell asleep side by side.

16
00:01:45.837 --> 00:01:50.877
Meg could not have chosen a more perfect day for the wedding.

17
00:01:50.878 --> 00:01:59.271
The sun was out bright and early while a gentle, light breeze pushed away the heat to make the temperature ideal for an outdoor ceremony.

18
00:01:59.272 --> 00:02:07.412
Due to their tight budget, Meg and John had planned a small, intimate wedding, inviting only family and a few close friends.

19
00:02:07.413 --> 00:02:14.265
Among the guests was Sallie Gardiner, Meg's close friend, who had married Ned Moffat a few months before.

20
00:02:14.266 --> 00:02:21.793
Sallie had had a lavish, elegant wedding, but Meg's simple yet warm ceremony was just as memorable.

21
00:02:21.794 --> 00:02:28.535
"Look at your tie, Brookes! It's a mess," Laurie cried, undoing the tie and re-doing it skillfully.

22
00:02:28.536 --> 00:02:32.982
"Thanks, Laurie, I'm a bit nervous," admitted his former tutor.

23
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:38.389
"That's understandable, considering today is the most important day of your life!

24
00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:43.125
But everything is going to be fine," reassured his grown-up pupil.

25
00:02:43.126 --> 00:02:48.572
Beth came out wearing a light blue silk dress and pink flowers in her hair.

26
00:02:48.573 --> 00:02:54.041
She sat down at the piano that was brought out especially for the occasion and began playing.

27
00:02:54.042 --> 00:03:02.133
Although Meg had wanted all three of her sisters to be bridesmaids, Beth was too nervous to walk down the aisle and have everyone stare at her.

28
00:03:02.134 --> 00:03:06.012
Instead, she offered to play the music for the wedding.

29
00:03:06.013 --> 00:03:11.710
Taking her cue, the guests found their seats and waited for the bride to enter.

30
00:03:11.711 --> 00:03:18.496
First Jo and Amy walked in together, each carrying a small bouquet, and wearing identical dresses to Beth's.

31
00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:21.708
The girls smiled as they walked down the aisle.

32
00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:26.403
"She's so beautiful," Laurie murmured as the girls passed him.

33
00:03:26.404 --> 00:03:34.217
"That Amy is going to break many hearts," replied Sallie, thinking Laurie was talking about the youngest March sisters.

34
00:03:34.218 --> 00:03:40.336
Laurie, however, was not referring to Amy; his eyes and heart were set on the other sister.

35
00:03:40.337 --> 00:03:44.361
Finally, the bride walked down the aisle with her father.

36
00:03:44.362 --> 00:03:52.969
Meg looked radiant in her white gown. She wore white daisies in her hair and held a simple bouquet of flowers in her hand.

37
00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:58.293
It was her smile, however, that lit up her face and illuminated her joy.

38
00:03:58.294 --> 00:04:08.350
The ceremony was short. Once Meg and John had exchanged their vows and rings, Mr. and Mrs. Brookes presented themselves to their guests.

39
00:04:08.351 --> 00:04:15.935
"Congratulations to you both!" Cheers and best wishes for the new couple were heard throughout the reception.

40
00:04:15.936 --> 00:04:20.901
Jo, having endured starvation for as long as her body would permit,

41
00:04:20.902 --> 00:04:28.366
could no longer neglect her rumbling stomach and purposefully made her way to the buffet table to indulge to her heart's content.

42
00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:32.123
Following closely behind like a lovesick puppy was Laurie.

43
00:04:32.124 --> 00:04:36.962
"Jo, you look amazing," he kept saying, much to her annoyance.

44
00:04:36.963 --> 00:04:43.623
"If you wore this dress and put this paint on your face, Laurie," Jo said, indicating her gown and makeup,

45
00:04:43.624 --> 00:04:47.851
"you'd be gorgeous too. Now, stop embarrassing me and go away."

46
00:04:47.852 --> 00:04:54.826
Laurie was not easily discouraged and would have gone on, if not for the entrance of an uninvited guest.

47
00:04:54.827 --> 00:05:04.518
"Josephine!" Aunt March's voice shrilled loudly, causing everyone to stop mid-conversation and frightening Beth so that she stopped playing her music.

48
00:05:04.519 --> 00:05:10.321
Jo nearly dropped her plate because Aunt March was the last person she expected to see.

49
00:05:10.322 --> 00:05:19.724
"Where is she? Where is your sister?" Aunt March demanded, briskly walking toward Jo and Laurie with determination.

50
00:05:19.725 --> 00:05:27.880
"I'm here, Aunt March," Meg boldly called out and cautiously approached her aunt, while John followed closely behind.

51
00:05:27.881 --> 00:05:31.656
Aunt March did not speak until Meg stood before her.

52
00:05:31.657 --> 00:05:35.505
When she arrived, the old woman scrutinized her from head to toe.

53
00:05:35.506 --> 00:05:40.817
"Yes, yes, all very simple like you," Aunt March snapped.

54
00:05:40.818 --> 00:05:47.085
John opened his mouth to defend his wife but Meg gently placed her hand on his arm to silence him.

55
00:05:47.086 --> 00:05:54.518
Since their last encounter, which had ended so disastrously, Meg had not spoken to her aunt for the past three years.

56
00:05:54.519 --> 00:05:58.475
"What can I do for you, Aunt March?" Meg asked calmly.

57
00:05:58.476 --> 00:06:04.518
"I've come to give you your wedding gift," Aunt March said, holding out a white envelope.

58
00:06:04.519 --> 00:06:10.096
"Aunt March, it isn't necessary for you to give a gift," Meg said graciously but firmly.

59
00:06:10.097 --> 00:06:19.714
Aunt March peered at Meg, then softening a little she said, "I know I uttered words that I shouldn't have and I regret them deeply.

60
00:06:19.715 --> 00:06:25.163
You are my only living relatives . . . ," she choked up but continued,

61
00:06:25.164 --> 00:06:31.814
"and I would like nothing more than to make the best use of my time on earth while I can."

62
00:06:31.815 --> 00:06:36.758
Mrs. Brookes warmly embraced her old aunt and gave her a tender kiss saying,

63
00:06:36.759 --> 00:06:43.691
"Thank you, Aunt March, for helping my husband and me start our married life at peace with our loved ones."

64
00:06:43.692 --> 00:06:49.288
Appropriately, Beth started up the music again and everyone laughed and danced merrily.

65
00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:55.605
"Do you think they'll be happy?" Jo asked Laurie as they watched her sister and brother-in-law dance.

66
00:06:55.606 --> 00:07:00.784
"Naturally," Laurie replied. "They are, after all, in love."

67
00:07:00.785 --> 00:07:06.785
Snorting, Jo remarked, "I think love is rather silly."

68
00:07:06.786 --> 00:07:10.595
Laurie held his tongue, but he disagreed.

69
00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:18.467
After hours of celebrating, Meg and John were ready to go to their new home, just down the street from her family's house.

70
00:07:18.468 --> 00:07:24.669
"Well, here we are," John said, stopping in front of their small modest house.

71
00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:30.392
"It's not as cozy as your place or as grand as the Laurence mansion but it's ours."

72
00:07:30.393 --> 00:07:40.293
Taking his arm in hers, Meg smiled at him and said, "Yes, it's our home, sweet home."
